## AI Page Builder V2 — System Rules

### CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE PATTERNS

#### Pattern 1: Server-Component Data Loading (NO BLANK EDITOR)
- `app/(editor)/edit/[slug]/page.tsx` MUST be async server component
- Call `getPageBySlug(params.slug)` BEFORE rendering editor
- Pass `initialData` from server to client component
- Client `<PuckEditor initialData={...} />` receives pre-loaded state
- NEVER pass `data={{}}` or undefined — always have valid Puck data shape

#### Pattern 2: resolveData for CMS Sync (NO STALE CONTENT)
- Use `resolveData` callback in Puck config for external data
- Check `changed.fieldName` to avoid re-fetching on every render
- Mark `readOnly: true` when field is CMS-driven
- On public render (`app/(frontend)/[slug]/page.tsx`), call `resolveAllData(data, config)` server-side
- This ensures published pages show fresh CMS data

#### Pattern 3: Genkit Flow Validation (NO INVALID BLOCKS)
- Derive `availableBlocks` from `Object.keys(puckConfig.components)` at runtime
- Use `z.enum(availableBlocks)` NOT `z.string()` for component names
- Always validate AI output before dispatching to Puck
- Filter page output: `content.filter(c => c.type in puckConfig.components)`
- Return `emptyPage` fallback if AI fails

#### Pattern 4: Supabase RLS (NO SECURITY BREACHES)
- Enable RLS on ALL tables
- Published pages: `FOR SELECT USING (published = true OR auth.role() = 'authenticated')`
- User pages: `FOR ALL USING (created_by = auth.uid())`
- Media: public read, authenticated upload
- Test policies in Supabase dashboard under "Authentication > Policies"

#### Pattern 5: API Validation (NO BAD DATA IN DB)
- Use Zod schemas on ALL routes (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE)
- Validate request body before DB insert
- Return 400 with schema errors if invalid
- Example: `SavePageSchema = z.object({ slug, title, data: PuckDataSchema })`

### CODE ORGANIZATION

**Blocks Folder Pattern**
```
lib/puck/blocks/
├── HeroBlock.tsx         → export HeroBlock + heroBlockFields
├── CardGridBlock.tsx     → export CardGridBlock + cardGridFields
└── ... (all blocks)

Naming:
- Component: PascalCase (HeroBlock)
- Fields export: camelCase + "Fields" (heroBlockFields)
- Import in config: import { HeroBlock, heroBlockFields } from "./blocks/HeroBlock"
```

**GenKit Flows Pattern**
```
lib/genkit/flows/
├── generateBlock.ts      → ai.defineFlow({ name, inputSchema, outputSchema }, handler)
├── generatePage.ts       → full page from description
├── editBlock.ts          → refine existing props
└── API routes auto-wrap with genkit appRoute

Every flow MUST:
- Accept typed input (Zod schema)
- Return typed output (Zod schema)
- Validate before returning
- Have OutputSchema with enums not strings for IDs/types
```

**DB Pattern**
```
lib/db/
├── supabase.ts           → clients (admin + public)
├── pages.ts              → CRUD (getPageBySlug, createPage, updatePage, etc.)
├── media.ts              → upload, sign URLs, delete
├── schema.ts             → Drizzle schema definitions
└── types.ts              → TypeScript types matching Supabase tables

Every function:
- Returns typed Promise<T | null>
- Handles errors + logs them
- Uses supabase admin for sensitive ops
- Uses supabase public for user-initiated ops
```

### FILE LOCATIONS (SACRED)

- Entry points: `app/` directory (Next.js convention)
- Server functions: `app/api/`, `lib/db/`, Supabase RLS
- Client components: `components/`, marked "use client"
- Types: `types/`, exported as modules
- Hooks: `lib/hooks/`, named `use*`
- Utilities: `lib/`
- Configuration: root level (tailwind, tsconfig, next.config)
- SQL: `sql/` directory
- Environment: `.env.local` (git-ignored)

### DISPATCH PATTERNS (PUCK ONLY)

- `dispatch({ type: "INSERT", componentType: string, destinationIndex: number, id: string })`
- `dispatch({ type: "SET_DATA", data: Data })`
- `dispatch({ type: "REMOVE", id: string })`
- `dispatch({ type: "MOVE", sourceIndex, destinationIndex, sourceZone?, destinationZone? })`

Never:
- Manipulate data.content directly, use dispatch
- Update props without validating shape first
- Render Puck inside Suspense without proper boundaries

### AUTHENTICATION & RLS

- Supabase Auth is the source of truth
- Call `supabase.auth.getSession()` to check logged-in state
- Middleware: verify auth on protected routes
- API routes: use `req.user` from auth context
- Supabase RLS: first line of defense, always enable

### DATA SHAPES (CANONICAL)

**Puck Data**
```typescript
{
  content: Array<{ type: string, props: Record<string, unknown>, readOnly?: Record<string, boolean> }>,
  root: { props: { title: string, description?: string } },
  zones?: { [zoneId: string]: content[] }
}
```

**Page Record (Supabase)**
```typescript
{
  id: UUID,
  slug: string,
  title: string,
  description?: string,
  data: JSONB,  // Puck data above
  published: boolean,
  published_at?: timestamp,
  created_by: UUID,
  updated_by: UUID,
  created_at: timestamp,
  updated_at: timestamp,
  deleted_at?: timestamp
}
```

**GenKit Output**
```typescript
{
  componentName: "HeroBlock" | "CardGridBlock" | ... (enum, never string),
  props: { ... },  // typed to block's AllBlockProps[componentName]
  reasoning?: string
}
```

### SECURITY CHECKLIST

- [ ] Supabase RLS enabled on all tables
- [ ] API routes validate input with Zod
- [ ] Sensitive ops (uploads) require auth
- [ ] API keys server-only (env.local, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*)
- [ ] GEMINI_API_KEY not exposed to client
- [ ] User strings sanitized with DOMPurify before render
- [ ] Rate limiting on `/api/ai/*` routes
- [ ] CORS configured for your domain only
- [ ] Audit logs track all page changes

### HOOKS PATTERN

```typescript
// lib/hooks/use*.ts
export function useMyHook() {
  const { dispatch } = usePuck();  // from @measured/puck
  const supabase = useSupabase();  // custom hook
  // ... logic ...
  return { data, loading, error };
}
```

Exported hooks:
- `useSupabase()` — auth + client
- `usePuckData(slug)` — load + sync
- `usePageSync(pageId)` — realtime updates
- `useMediaUpload()` — upload to storage
- `useTheme()` — current theme

### TESTING CHECKLIST

Before deploying:
1. [ ] Create new page `/edit/test-123`
2. [ ] Add blocks via Puck visual editor
3. [ ] Test AI block generation (AIPanel)
4. [ ] Test AI full page generation
5. [ ] Save page (PUT /api/pages/[slug])
6. [ ] Publish page
7. [ ] View public page (should resolve external data)
8. [ ] Restore from version history
9. [ ] Upload image to media
10. [ ] Test on mobile (responsive)

### COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID

❌ Passing `data={{}}` to PuckEditor
✅ Load from server: `await getPageBySlug(slug)`

❌ Fetching external data inside block render
✅ Use `resolveData` callback in config

❌ Accepting string for component type in GenKit
✅ Use `z.enum(AVAILABLE_BLOCKS)`

❌ Not validating AI output before dispatch
✅ Always `safeParse()` then check

❌ Forgetting RLS on new tables
✅ `ALTER TABLE x ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` + policies

❌ Hardcoding database credentials
✅ Use env variables only

---

**This ruleset ensures consistency, prevents data-loading bugs, and maintains security across the entire system.**
